    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (82.08) and **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) anchoring the offense, standing as our premier starts. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a porous matchup against M\u00e1rquez (5.64 xERA), and despite a minor drag from the opposing catcher's efficiency, his elite speed profile keeps his floor comfortably high. **Seiya Suzuki** is arguably our highest-upside play due to a massive +16% park adjustment and a generous +13% boost from facing a mid-tier arm in Baz; however, managers must monitor the 45% rain risk, as any delay could jeopardize his impact. **James Wood** (72.06) rounds out the tier-one options, leveraging an elite .424 xwOBA and an aggressive +10% batting order boost to capitalize on a favorable matchup against Imai.\n\nThe benching process was particularly rigorous today, with **Max Muncy** (43.15) serving as the most difficult omission. While **Max Muncy** receives a park-based boost, the severe drag of facing Skubal (2.74 xERA)\u2014which resulted in a -19% SP skill penalty\u2014rendered him too inefficient to crack the active lineup. Elsewhere, **Kyle Karros** (61.17) earns a spot over alternatives because of his +7% platoon edge and, crucially, a slow pitcher delivery that signals a prime opportunity for a stolen base. Finally, be advised that while **Mickey Moniak** (50.11) and **Zach McKinstry** (52.08) remain in the lineup, both hover near our marginal start threshold; their value is buoyed by specific platoon splits against Wrobleski and Ginn, but they remain at risk of being replaced should late-game lineup pivots or pinch-hit scenarios arise.",
